      "is_risk": true,
      "conviction": null,
      "raw_mention": "Twenty One Capital",
      "text": "Twenty One Capital is now worth less than the bitcoin sitting on its own balance sheet, per BeInCrypto. The whole treasury-company thing ran on one loop: issue stock above NAV, buy more coin, repeat. Below NAV that loop doesn't just stall, it inverts — the accretive move becomes selling coin to buy back your own shares. I don't know how fast that actually happens in practice, or whether these boards will do it at all before they have to. But for two years these companies were the permanent bid under bitcoin, and nobody's really sat with what the other side of that looks like.",
